    "note": "The reduction case. The arrow starts on the boron to hydrogen BOND, not on a lone pair, because the hydride is a bonding pair being handed over and the hydrogen has no lone pair to give. The arrow pivots on the migrating hydrogen, which is the same shape as a 1,2 hydride shift in chem-core legality.ts. The transferred hydrogen is explicit and the other three on boron stay implicit, because only one of the four moves and no arrow can express a change in an implicit count. Boron ends the first step neutral with six valence electrons, which is borane, and that is correct rather than a valence failure."
